      }), ". Imagine a hotel check-in desk where the main ledger is the database file and the WAL is a sticky-note pad next to it. Reads check both: the main ledger and any sticky notes that modify the rows being read. Writes go to the sticky notes first. Periodically (at a checkpoint), the sticky notes are folded back into the main ledger. This model explains why readers and the single writer can proceed concurrently: they are working from different layers of the same data."]
